Hey, my name is **Abizar Tiki Wala**, and this is my new project.

This project is a **Construction Material Guide** built using **Corrective Retrieval-Augmented Generation (Corrective RAG)**.

The application is designed to help users find relevant information about construction materials and provide accurate, context-aware responses based on the available knowledge base.

The project uses a retrieval-based approach to search for relevant information before generating a response. Corrective RAG is used to improve the retrieval process by evaluating the retrieved information and correcting the workflow when the retrieved results are not sufficiently relevant.

The goal of this project is to explore and implement **RAG pipelines, document retrieval, vector databases, embeddings, and Large Language Models (LLMs)** in a practical real-world use case.

## Current Progress

### Completed

* Project setup and folder structure
* PDF document loading using `PyPDFLoader`
* Document processing and text extraction
* Text chunking using `RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter`
* Configured chunk size and chunk overlap
* Embedding generation using Hugging Face embeddings
* Vector Store implementation using **Typesense**
* Retriever setup using Typesense Vector Store
* Prompt Template implementation for passing retrieved context and user questions to the LLM

### In Progress

* Corrective RAG implementation
* LLM integration
* Connecting Retriever → Prompt Template → LLM
* Final response generation
* Streamlit interface

### Next Steps

* Implement document relevance evaluation
* Add corrective retrieval when retrieved context is insufficient
* Integrate the LLM with the RAG pipeline
* Build the Streamlit chatbot interface
* Test the complete end-to-end pipeline


Wait for some days, all the modules will be updated
